[3855]={"'You have returned! I trust that you have brought your report on the infected creatures of Agarnaith?'\
\
You tell Tancram what you observed, and he notes your observations on a small piece of parchment.\
\
'Thank you for this, ${PLAYER}. Gondor needs as much information about the spread of this disease as can be obtained. Come back tomorrow for more work, my friend.'","Tancram is in the Hall of the King.","'I have heard the worries of Mithrandir and others concerning some foul disease that spreads within the swamps of Agarnaith. I ask that you defeat the boars and wolves that you find there, for the disease has caused them to engage in a frenzied madness.\
\
'I ask too that you <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at a number of infected creatures and provide your opinion on the disease's spread. I am interested especially in plague-flies, bog-lurkers, gore-crows, and infectious plague-rats. Good luck to you, ${PLAYER}, and know that you will be rewarded for your observations.'","Daily Request: A Casual Study","Defeated Plagued Dire-wolves in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You mark the spread of the disease in the bog-lurker","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at an Infectious Plague-rat in Agarnaith","You mark the spread of the disease in the plague-rat","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at an Agarnaith Gore-crow","Defeated Diseased Swamp-boars in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If your travels will take you to Agarnaith, I have something with which you could help me. I have heard the worries of Mithrandir and others concerning some foul disease that spreads within the swamps of Agarnaith. I ask that you defeat the boars and wolves that you find there, for the disease has caused them to engage in a frenzied madness.\
\
'I ask too that you <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at a number of infected creatures and provide your opinion on the disease's spread. I am interested especially in plague-flies, bog-lurkers, gore-crows, and infectious plague-rats. Good luck to you, ${PLAYER}, and know that you will be rewarded for your observations.'","Bring your report on the spread of the disease to Tancram in the Hall of the King","You mark the spread of the disease in the plague-fly","Defeat Diseased Swamp-boars in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Plagued Dire-wolves in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tancram has asked you to perform a casual study of some of the creatures that crawl or fly in plague-ridden Agarnaith.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at a Bloody Bog-lurker in Agarnaith","You mark the spread of the disease in the gore-crow","Tancram has asked you to defeat boars and wolves in plague-ridden Agarnaith, and to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at several other creatures in order to gauge the spread of the disease.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at a Bloody Plague-fly in Agarnaith"},
[3856]={"Defeat enemies in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, you have a package for me from Vétha? What has my wife sent me this time?'\
\
Góthur carefully unfolds the leather satchel and removes a parchment covered with precise, angular runes. He is about to show it to you, but suddenly he flushes and keeps it to himself.\
\
'My temperature rises. It must be the lake of fire! Yes, that must be it. This message from my wife is not intended for anyone's eyes but my own, ${PLAYER}! I thank you for the delivery, and I thank you doubly-so for not reading it!'","'You delivered the package to Góthur? I hope that is enough for Vétha, but I am not foolish enough to believe she will not have another one to send him in a few days!\
\
'Perhaps you will come back in a day or two and deliver that one as well? And the one after that? By Durin's Beard! When will Góthur return home and put an end to all this package delivering? Not soon enough, that much is clear, ${PLAYER}!'","'Ah, you have a package for me from Vétha? What has my wife sent me this time?'\
\
Góthur carefully unfolds the leather satchel and removes a small, but very shiny, stone, and a piece of parchment.\
\
'This is a small nugget of gold. Ah! My son Gárni has been learning the basics of mining, and this is one of the early results! The ore does not appear far from the vein, does it not? My son will be a fine prospector indeed if he is already so adept at such a young age!\
\
'Nay, he will be even better than I, for I did not have much of a taste for mining. Is that not why I chose the adventuring life? Still, I am so proud of him for surpassing me in this, and already! Thank you for bringing me this, ${PLAYER}!'","Talk to Vórthi in the Hall Under the Mountain","'Ah, you have a package for me from Vétha? What has my wife sent me this time?'\
\
Góthur carefully unfolds the leather satchel and removes a parchment with a charcoal drawing on it. He studies it for a moment and then smiles.\
\
'A drawing of the Lonely Mountain! My son Gárni has become quite the artist, has he not? Look at this fine representation of the Mountain, ${PLAYER}! My son is quite an artist!'\
\
Góthur tilts his head to the side and studies the drawing more carefully.\
\
'Oh, wait a moment. I see now that my wife has written her name in the corner. Vétha drew this picture for me. Well, it is quite good, is it not? She is as fine an artist as her beard is long, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for bringing this to me, and I look forward to what you might bring next time!'","Defeated enemies in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Góthur is by a lake of fire to the south-west of Mordath, the great pit over which Barad-dûr once towered.","Daily Request: A Package from Home","Vórthi asked you to defeat foes in Dor Amarth before delivering the package to Góthur.","'You defeated some of the foes throughout Dor Amarth? I suppose that is enough, and now you can deliver the package from his wife to Góthur. He should be near a lake of fire south-west of the ruins of Barad-dûr, in Dor Amarth.'","'Ah, you have a package for me from Vétha? What has my wife sent me this time?'\
\
Góthur carefully unfolds the leather satchel and removes a parchment with a brief message written in a messy hand.\
\
'It is a message from my son, Gárni! He misses me, and has written to wish me well as I adventure in... well, he has not mastered his runes as of yet, but I believe this word is intended to represent Gorgoroth. See how he began writing it, but did not know when to stop? Ah, he is clever, more clever than me by far!\
\
'He has asked what he always asks: he wants to know about the monsters I have encountered in this land. He is still too young to hear about them in all their beastly glory, but one day I will return and have many fine stories to tell. Vétha may not like it, but I know that it will whet Gárni's appetite for adventure! Who knows? One day he too may journey in this land, and he too may have a son who desires to hear tales of it! Wouldn't that be something?'","Vórthi has given you a package to deliver to an adventurer in Dor Amarth.","'Durin's Folk are a very sturdy, heroic people, no strangers to adventure. But the Black Land of Mordor is shrouded in mystery, and no one really knows what to expect.\
\
'Our adventurers have not balked at crossing the Mountains of Shadow and exploring the plateau of Gorgoroth, but their families do not always share in their boldness. One of our scouts, Góthur, adventures in Dor Amarth and has faced many dangers there already. His wife Vétha has prepared a package for him, and insists that someone deliver it to him. It seems to me that every week she has a new package to send him, but I do not want to tell her this cannot be done, ${PLAYER}. Will you bring this week's package to Góthur? Before you deliver it, perhaps you can defeat foes in Dor Amarth? That way there will be some justification for making the journey!\
\
'Góthur should be near a lake of fire south-west of Mordath, in Dor Amarth.'","'Ah, you have a package for me from Vétha? What has my wife sent me this time?'\
\
Góthur carefully unfolds the leather satchel and removes a parchment covered in tiny, angular letters. He studies it for a moment and then sighs.\
\
'Gossip from home, ${PLAYER}. There is a lot of talk of our neighbours, rumours of the king, assorted petty grievances and hurts, and the family's minor triumphs and accomplishments. I do not think I will read it all right now, and it would be of no interest to you, but it does achieve two useful things. First, it helps Vétha pass the time while I am away, for it takes her a long time to write all this out. Second, it helps me pass the time when boredom threatens, even here in Mordor. And so such gossip helps to pass twice as much time!\
\
'I have had a lot of time to think up this justification, my friend, for while I enjoy news from home, there's always just so very much of it. It is rather exhausting. At any rate, I thank you for bringing it to me! Perhaps I will see you again.'","Deliver the package from Vétha to Góthur","Vórthi is in the Hall Under the Mountain, in Erebor.","'Ah, you have a package for me from Vétha? What has my wife sent me this time?'\
\
Góthur carefully unfolds the leather satchel and removes a smooth, round ball. With an exclamation of delight, he brandishes it in your direction.\
\
'This is a loaf of cram, ${PLAYER}, as the Men of Dale are wont to make, but they did not bake this one. No, my wife Vétha has sought to learn their recipe and has made some improvements to it. This one is tougher and hardier than others of its type... much like my Vétha, as she would be the first to tell you!\
\
'Thank you, my friend! I would offer you a bite, but surely you need to be off on your own adventures; I do not wish to keep you from them for as long as consuming a serving of this cram would take!'","'One of our scouts, Góthur, adventures in Dor Amarth and has faced many dangers there already. His wife Vétha has prepared a package for him, and insists that someone deliver it to him. It seems to me that every week she has a new package to send him, but I do not want to tell her this cannot be done, ${PLAYER}. Will you bring this week's package to Góthur? Before you deliver it, perhaps you can defeat foes in Dor Amarth? That way there will be some justification for making the journey!\
\
'Góthur should be near a lake of fire south-west of Mordath, in Dor Amarth.'"},
[3857]={"Collect Easterling food jars in Rhûd Vorn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hello there, ${PLAYER}. I have been collecting requests in order to determine how best we can help our friends and neighbours, but today the request is from one Aster Hayward. Yes, this request is my own!\
\
'You see, a number of former prisoners have been freed from the yoke of slavery in Gorgoroth, and now they seek to make homes for themselves in Gondor. Many of these freed slaves are Nurnhoth, the people of Nurn, to the south. I have not studied their family trees as sufficiently as I would like, for while I am a student of lineage and ancestry, my specialty is in that of the larger hobbit families of the Shire. Still, I understand that the Nurnhoth are of Easterling descent, and have Easterling customs and habits.\
\
'This is a long way of saying that many of the freed Nurnhoth have different tastes than the rest of us, and while they have freedom they still lack some of the things that would make them most comfortable. I speak of food, ${PLAYER}! I have conversed with some of them, and have learned that they would enjoy a few traditional meals: Khingal, Lavang, and Pishi Badam, which they have described to me but I have never sampled. We do not have the ingredients for these meals, but we might take them from some of the Easterlings in Gorgoroth who are hostile to us. Deprive the Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, on the eastern side of the vale of Udûn, of their food jars, and I may be able to cook up some of these meals for the freed Nurnhoth. I want them to feel welcome, ${PLAYER}, and this may help them feel more at home!'","Aster Hayward wants to provide meals for some of the freed Nurnhoth and has asked you to collect some of the foodstuffs she thinks they would enjoy.","Food jars can be found at Rhûd Vorn, an Easterling camp on the eastern side of Udûn.","Bring the food jars to Aster Hayward in Tham Periain","'Deprive the Easterlings at Rhûd Vorn, on the eastern side of the vale of Udûn, of their food jars, and I may be able to cook up some of these meals for the freed Nurnhoth. I want them to feel welcome, ${PLAYER}, and this may help them feel more at home!'","'Thank you for these food jars, ${PLAYER}! I will open them up and make a catalog of the ingredients we have obtained, and will set about learning how to cook up some of the meals the freed Nurnhoth mentioned to me! I hope they are not too difficult to make, but even if they are it will all be worth it if the freed Nurnhoth enjoy having a taste of home!\
\
'Come back tomorrow and I should have another request for you, friend!'","Daily Request: An Errand for Aster","Collected Easterling food jars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aster Hayward is in Tham Periain."},
[3859]={"Collect travelling seeds from nerbyg and plague-flies in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have returned with the seeds and the weeds that Meriadoc requested? I will bring them to him. I hope he finds more joy in these than in the last batch of plant-matter with which he filled his pipe. That smoke did not suit him at all, and I can still smell the choking fumes in my memory, if not with my nose.\
\
'At least there are fewer foul creatures to threaten wanderers in the swamp. Come back tomorrow and I will have another request for you!'","Bring the items you collected to Aster Hayward in Tham Periain","Aster Hayward conveyed a request to you from Meriadoc Brandybuck, who desires to continue his research into plants and vegetation, particularly for use in his pipe.","Collect entangled weeds from bog-lurkers in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aster Hayward is in Tham Periain.","Daily Request: An Errand for Merry","In the swamps of Agarnaith, travelling seeds can be found from nerbyg and plague-flies, and entangled weeds can be found from bog-lurkers.","Collected entangled weeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Meriadoc Brandybuck has heard from other adventurers that the nerbyg and flies that inhabit Agarnaith sometimes pick up seeds from distant shores, carrying them on long journeys far from the pods at which they began. He has heard too that the spindly legs of bog-lurkers often catch on weeds growing out of river-banks, pulling them free of their moorings and carrying them long miles. He has asked that you collect these travelling seeds and entangled weeds and bring them back for his study.'","Collected travelling seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have asked our friends to suggest tasks for adventurers to undertake within Gorgoroth, and they have been very kind as to offer several requests. I spoke with Meriadoc Brandybuck mere moments ago, and he told me he desires to continue his research into the various properties and classifications of plants and other herbs. His interest is chiefly in those plants that can be put to use in his pipe, and he is always seeking new such vegetation.\
\
'It seems he has heard from other adventurers that the nerbyg and flies that inhabit Agarnaith sometimes pick up seeds from distant shores, carrying them on long journeys far from the pods at which they began. He has heard too that the spindly legs of bog-lurkers often catch on weeds growing out of river-banks, pulling them free of their moorings and carrying them long miles. Meriadoc has asked that you collect these travelling seeds and entangled weeds and bring them back for his study.\
\
'I suppose a botanical interest is sufficient for this purpose, and if it is not... well, at least you will be thinning the numbers of these creatures that might otherwise pose a threat to adventurers in the swamp.'"},
[3861]={"Defeat spiders in Lhingris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aster Hayward conveyed a request to you from Samwise Gamgee: to defeat spiders in Lhingris.","'Did you make a dent in the number of spiders that crawl about Lhingris? Even a small one? I am sure it will be of help, even if there are always more eight-legged beasts to replace the ones you squished. It is still a good thing to do!\
\
'Come back tomorrow and I will have another request for you to undertake. I will give Samwise a break for now! He does not like thinking up these tasks, poor thing. He has my sympathy for a short while, but then I will need another, and then he will not be allowed off the hook!'","'Samwise asks that adventurers defeat spiders in Lhingris, where there is no shortage of the things. He is quite upset about the spiders, for some reason, but he would not tell me why. At any rate, it will be a helpful errand. Fulfill this request and I will have a reward for you! Samwise's own reward is that I will not bother him for another request for some days!'","Defeated spiders in Lhingris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have been collecting requests from our friends concerning how best we can help our neighbours in this land, and today's request is from Samwise.\
\
'He was reluctant to ask anything of me, and it took a good deal of prodding before he eventually consented to give me a request. Still, if the others can provide me with tasks to dole out to willing adventurers, there's no reason for a Gamgee to be exempted!\
\
'Eventually he relented, and provided me with a request. It is a simple one and quite straightforward, although the execution of it will be anything but, if the rumours I have heard are true! Samwise asks that adventurers defeat spiders in Lhingris, where there is no shortage of the things. He is quite upset about the spiders, for some reason, but he would not tell me why. At any rate, it will be a helpful errand. Fulfill this request and I will have a reward for you! Samwise's own reward is that I will not bother him for another request for some days!'","Spiders can be found in great numbers throughout Lhingris.","Daily Request: An Errand for Sam","Talk to Aster Hayward in Tham Periain","Aster Hayward is in Tham Periain."},
[3862]={"The Sons of Stone are located on the road near Rath Cail in Lhingris.","You remove a bundle of equipment from the waggon","The Crow-feeders are located on the road south of Rath Cail in Lhingris.","'I will take it from here, ${PLAYER}, and distribute the remaining equipment to other adventurers within Lhingris.\
\
'Perhaps I will see you another time! There is always more to be done!'","Find the Crow-feeders and supply the dwarves with fresh equipment","Find the Sons of Stone and supply the dwarves with fresh equipment","'The conquest of Gorgoroth continues! How can it not end in triumph, when Durin's Folk have so many fine heroes setting forth from Erebor? Several bands of great renown have made the journey, and their names are well-known to all dwarves: the Sons of Stone and the Crow-feeders, whose adventures are legendary.\
\
'But without new weapons and armour, even they cannot hope to prevail! They must be reinforced with fresh equipment, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'My friend Vágrek has a cart full of crafted weapons and armour, and he has driven it to Lhingris. Unload his cart on the road in the north-east of that web-choked valley, and find the Sons of Stone and the Crow-feeders south along the road, near Rath Cail and slightly beyond.'","Vórthi has asked for your help rearming a number of dwarves adventuring in Lhingris.","Bring the remaining equipment to Unvíth just north of the Crow-feeders","Unload the cart on the road in the north-east of Lhingris, near the entrance to Dor Amarth","Vágrek is with his cart in the north-east of Lhingris, near the road into Dor Amarth.","The Crow-feeders have been resupplied with new equipment","'My friend Vágrek has a cart full of crafted weapons and armour, and he has driven it to Lhingris. Unload his cart on the road in the north-east of that web-choked valley, and find the Sons of Stone and the Crow-feeders south along the road, near Rath Cail and slightly beyond.'","The Sons of Stone have been resupplied with new equipment","Daily Request: Arming Our Warriors","Unvíth is just north of the Crow-feeders."},
[3863]={"'Face foes in Dor Amarth, either rock-worms or dire-horns, and fight them on behalf of the Elves.\
\
'If it were me, I would defeat whichever enemies first crossed my path, and I encourage you to do the same. Once you have made your choice and thinned the ranks of our enemies, return to me and be rewarded.'","Glórellas is in the Court of Celeborn.","Defeated rock-worms or fire grims in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Daily Request: Choosing Doom","Defeat rock-worms or fire grims in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Glórellas has asked you to defeat some of the foes that stalk Dor Amarth, but she left the choice of which foes to face up to you.","'You have my thanks and those of the Lord and Lady as well, for the Doomfold of Dor Amarth is hazardous and possessed of many dangers. Those that adventure there will now be safer for your efforts on their behalf.\
\
'Return tomorrow and there will be further means by which you may aid us.'","Glórellas asked you to defeat foes in Dor Amarth, choosing between rock-worms, dire-horns, and a number of other creatures, in order to aid the Elves that fight in that land.","Talk to Glórellas in the Court of Celeborn","Defeated dire-horns, sûlokil, or fire-drakes in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Many Elves fight in Dor Amarth, as they did of old, and any aid you can lend to them will be appreciated. It is of no matter to me which of the foes there you face, whether it be rock-worms or dire-horns, just that you fight them on our behalf.\
\
'If it were me, I would defeat whichever enemies first crossed my path, and I encourage you to do the same. Once you have made your choice and thinned the ranks of our enemies, return to me and be rewarded.'","Defeat dire-horns, sûlokil, or fire-drakes in Dor Amarth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[3866]={"The keg is greatly appreciated!","Vórthi has heard tales of the great lake of fire in Talath Úrui, the Ghâshghurm, and wants you to bring some means of refreshment to the dwarves that must adventure by its banks.","Set up a keg for parched dwarves north of the road between Naerband and the Ghâshghurm","Talk to Vórthi in the Hall Under the Mountain","Set up a keg for parched dwarves east of Thorzhaf, in Talath Úrui","There is a good spot for a keg north of the road in Talath Úrui, between Naerband and the Ghâshghurm.","There is a good spot for a keg north-east of Thorzhaf, in Talath Úrui.","Vórthi is in the Hall Under the Mountain.","'I want to help the dwarves that still labour in Talath Úrui. I have prepared kegs of ale to quench the thirst they surely possess. Set up the kegs not far from the Ghâshghurm, perhaps north-east of Thorzhaf, off the road. Parched dwarves will be glad to see you!'","Set up a keg for parched dwarves north-east of Thorzhaf, in Talath Úrui","There is a good spot for a keg east of Thorzhaf, in Talath Úrui.","'Dwarves returning from Mordor have told tales of the Ghâshghurm, a great lake of fire that boils and bubbles south of Mount Doom. The picture these scorching stories paint is a most unpleasant one, and it makes my brow sweat even here, among the cool shadows under the Lonely Mountain!\
\
'I want to help the dwarves that still labour in Talath Úrui. I have prepared kegs of ale to quench the thirst they surely possess. Set up the kegs not far from the Ghâshghurm, perhaps north-east of Thorzhaf, off the road. Parched dwarves will be glad to see you!'","'Welcome back, friend! Were the dwarves in Talath Úrui glad to see you and the kegs of ale you brought with you? Yes! I am pleased to hear that!\
\
'I have helped our adventuring dwarves in many ways for the past few weeks, but I think I am most proud of this task. Thank you for helping me help our dwarf heroes! Adventuring is thirsty work... I speak from experience!'","Daily Request: Hot Work, And Lots Of It!"},
[3868]={"Tancram has asked you to raise banners of the King in the vale of Udûn.","'Bring these banners to the Doomfold of Dor Amarth, and raise them proudly. Begin north of Fushaum Tûm, along the road, and make your way east. There are two rivers of fire in that direction, and I think that you should raise some of the banners near them, though they be off the road. They will serve as a reminder to those fiends that Gondor remains ever-vigilant.'","This banner will serve as a reminder that a king rules in Gondor","Tancram is in the Hall of the King.","Raise banners of the King over Dor Amarth (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'You raised the banners of the King over Dor Amarth? Very good, my friend. How long will it be before we must raise more banners? The Orcs and other foul beasts of Gorgoroth have short memories, as I think I told you. They will always need reminding that a king rules once more in Gondor, and will not brook their defiance.'","Tancram gave you a number of banners to raise over Dor Amarth.","Daily Request: Notice of the King","Talk to Tancram in the Hall of the King","'The Orcs and foul creatures of Gorgoroth have short memories, ${PLAYER}. We need to remind them that a King once again rules in Gondor, and he will not stand idly by while they threaten to break the peace.\
\
'Bring these banners to the Doomfold of Dor Amarth, and raise them proudly. Begin north of Fushaum Tûm, along the road, and make your way east. There are two rivers of fire in that direction, and I think that you should raise some of the banners near them, though they be off the road. They will serve as a reminder to those fiends that Gondor remains ever-vigilant.'"},
[3869]={"Defeat crebain or sickle-flies in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vórthi has asked for your help combatting threats in Agarnaith, but he is not particular about how exactly you accomplish it.","'The swamp-lands of Agarnaith are full of danger, and any of the foes you face there will make that treacherous vale safer. Birds and bugs, wolves and boars, Orcs and Uruks... it makes no difference to me! Choose some foes to defeat, and defeat them! What could be simpler than that?'","Defeated boars or wolves in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orcs or Uruks in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Daily Request: Pick Your Poison","Defeated crebain or sickle-flies in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vórthi is in the Hall Under the Mountain.","Vórthi asked you to choose foes to defeat in Agarnaith, and no matter what you choose to face, you will be making the swamp more safe.","Defeat boars or wolves in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are looking to help Durin's Folk? I am glad to hear it, but I do not have any requests prepared. I am quite embarrassed to be caught this way... there must be something you can do!\
\
'Ah, I have it! The swamp-lands of Agarnaith are full of danger, and any of the foes you face there will make that treacherous vale safer. Birds and bugs, wolves and boars, Orcs and Uruks... it makes no difference to me! Choose some foes to defeat, and defeat them! What could be simpler than that?'","Defeated Orcs or Uruks in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are back, and Agarnaith is made more safe for your efforts? Well done. No, do not tell me what foes you defeated... there is no need for that! Whatever they were, they will not be a problem anymore! Ha ha ha!'","Talk to Vórthi in the Hall Under the Mountain"},
[3870]={"Glórellas asked you to defeat enemies in Talath Úrui before finding Candithil and obtaining his report.","Talk to Glórellas in the Court of Celeborn","'You are here for my report? Very well, but know that it looks to the future and not the past, and will be of limited use for those wishing to adventure in Talath Úrui.\
\
'The gate to the south-east is held against us, for the moment, but I have been trying to form a plan to seize control from our enemies. If we could but gain access to the gate of Ennyn Ûr, we might pass through into the lands of Nurn. What awaits us there? I will continue my excursions in Talath Úrui, but my eyes ever turn to the gate, and wonder what lies beyond that sealed fastness. Curiosity was always a weakness of mine, ${PLAYER}. I believe that is one of the qualities for which I was chosen to walk in Gorgoroth, but I do not know for certain.\
\
'Return with my report, and I hope one day you come back to me with a command from the Lord or Lady to pass beyond Ennyn Ûr!'","Glórellas has asked you to find Candithil in Talath Úrui and obtain his report.","'Thank you for the report, ${PLAYER}. Candithil continues to provide useful information concerning the situation in Talath Úrui. I hope he does not push his good fortune too far, but for now his adventures are of use to the Court of Lothlórien, and his daring is a credit to his people.\
\
'Come back to me tomorrow and I will have further responsibilities for you.'","'I ask that you defeat any of the hostile creatures that inhabit Talath Úrui. After doing so, if you find yourself near the cross-roads south-east of Orodruin, return to me with Candithil's report and be rewarded for your efforts.'","'You have come for my report? It is good you arrived when you did, for I am lately returned from my last excursion.\
\
'I climbed the slope of Orodruin, and crept as high as I could given the great devastation of the southern face. If you dare to go that way, you will find the footing treacherous and the climb quite dangerous. It was a worthwhile endeavour, however, for from that height I was able to observe the movements of many enemies.'\
\
Candithil relays the information to you. You commit it to memory and thank him for the report.","Talk to Candithil by the cross-roads south-east of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui","'If you find yourself near the cross-roads south-east of Orodruin, return to me with Candithil's report and be rewarded for your efforts.'","'Lord Celeborn dispatched scouts to many of the regions of Gorgoroth, and they journeyed to each side of Orodruin. We have received many of their reports in the last few days, but Candithil journeys in Talath Úrui, and his reports are sometimes delayed.\
\
'I ask that you defeat any of the hostile creatures that inhabit Talath Úrui. After doing so, if you find yourself near the cross-roads south-east of Orodruin, return to me with Candithil's report and be rewarded for your efforts.'","Candithil is near the cross-roads south-east of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui.","Daily Request: Report from Talath Úrui","Defeated hostile foes in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Glórellas is in the Court of Celeborn.","'You are here for my report? Today it is brief, for my excursion was short-lived.\
\
'I explored part of the way into Nargroth, the great fortress delved into the depths of the caverns to the north. It is a place of horror, full of Ghâsh-hai and spirits of flame. I mapped a portion of the fortress, but had to turn back before it was complete.\
\
'I hope to return in the days ahead and find more success.'","'You have come for my report? There is little to say of this land I have not already reported. Let this then be my account.\
\
'I miss the sun, ${PLAYER}, and the cool breezes of Lothlórien. I miss the greenery of my home: the plants, and the trees, and the flowers. This is a harsh and unforgiving land, blanketed by fire and smoke and the smell of sulfur. My mouth tastes of ashes. The weather is unchanging, or if it be changeable the difference is from disagreeable to distasteful; a small one only, and of little account to my eyes.\
\
'Return with my report. It should not be surprising, but perhaps my next will be of more use.'","'You are here for my report? Very well, but I warn you it may not be of much help, for I am still considering the significance of the behaviour I observed.\
\
'There is a town to the north-west of here, rent by a great river of flame that snakes from the summit of Orodruin. The inhabitants of that town war upon each other, north and south, finding no common cause with the other. It is a curiosity to me, but I hope this infighting may be turned to our advantage. It bears further study, but as of now I am unsure how best to capitalize upon this turmoil.'","Defeat hostile foes in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You are here for my report? I give it to you gladly.\
\
'From a small rise not far from here, I beheld a small group of Orcs bound for the prison-fortress of Naerband. Nurnhoth slaves were chained together in the centre of the marching lines. I could not leave them to their cruel fate; I nocked an arrow almost before I knew what I was doing, and let it fly only slightly after my mind caught up to my heart.\
\
'I left the captors where they fell, and sent the Nurnhoth along with friends of mine, to freedom. May they find happiness where at last they settle. That is my report.'"},
[3871]={"Tancram has asked you to defeat some of the dragon-kind that stalk Talath Úrui.","Defeated fire-drakes in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat fire-drakes in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Defeat salamanders and rock-worms in Talath Úrui, or hunt for the more dangerous fire-drakes that walk the scorching plains. I leave the decision up to you, for facing either of these will aid the Kingdom of Gondor.'","Daily Request: Scorching Selection","'Many are the dangerous foes that stalk the burning plains of Talath Úrui, but none are so threatening as the creatures of dragon-kind. Defeat salamanders and rock-worms, or hunt for the more dangerous fire-drakes that walk the scorching plains. I leave the decision up to you, for facing either of these will aid the Kingdom of Gondor.\
\
'Good luck to you, ${PLAYER}.'","Tancram is in the Hall of the King.","Defeated salamanders or rock-worms in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat salamanders or rock-worms in Talath Úrui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have defeated some of the dragon-kind in Talath Úrui? I am pleased to hear it, and offer you this reward from the Kingdom of Gondor in acknowledgement of the service you have provided.\
\
'Come back tomorrow for more work, my friend.'","Salamanders, rock-worms, and fire-drakes can be found throughout Talath Úrui.","Talk to Tancram in the Hall of the King"},
[3872]={"'A shield was given to me, a shield that was once cloven in two but has now been repaired with leather straps. I believe you know the man who lent it to me, for he has repaired a number of them and bears one himself.\
\
'It is a shield of the Thandrim, who once held the fortress of Durthand and were slain by the forces of Mordor. This man does not want the Orcs and other evil creatures who now inhabit it to forget the steadfast Thandrim, and he wishes for brave warriors to bear this shield to the keep once known as the Black Shield. He asks that you hang the shield upon a wall, and then defeat a number of foes within the fortress.\
\
'Once you have done this, retrieve the shield from the wall where you left it, and return it to me. This man will be glad to have the shield returned, but more than that: he will be glad to know that the memory of the Thandrim lives on, and can still strike out at their hated foes.'","Tancram asked you to defeat enemies within the fortress of Durthang, in Udûn.","Hang the repaired Thandrim shield on the wall outside the entrance to Durthang, in Udûn","Retrieve the shield of the Thandrim from the wall where you placed it","'Hang that shield upon a wall outside Durthang, and then defeat a number of foes within the fortress.\
\
'Once you have done this, retrieve the shield from the wall where you left it, and return it to me. This man will be glad to have the shield returned, but more than that: he will be glad to know that the memory of the Thandrim lives on, and can still strike out at their hated foes.'","Tancram has given you a shield of the Thandrim, now repaired, and has asked you to defeat the evil ones who hold Durthang.","Tancram gave you a shield to hang on a wall outside the entrance to Durthang, so you may fight in memory of the fallen Thandrim.","Daily Request: Still Defiant","'Thank you for returning the shield; I will ensure it is brought to the man to whom it belongs. It is a wonder to me that the Thandrim can still strike at their enemies, even now, a thousand years after their deaths.\
\
'We are their instrument in this: not of vengeance, but of justice. And of course you will be rewarded for the work. Come back tomorrow and there will be more work, and more reward!'","Tancram is in the Hall of the King.","The shield was untouched by enemies. Perhaps they fear it","Defeated enemies within Durthang in memory of the Thandrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You placed a repaired shield of the Thandrim on a wall outside the entrance to Durthang, in Udûn, and should now retrieve it.","Defeat enemies within Durthang in memory of the Thandrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the repaired Thandrim shield to Tancram in the Hall of the King"},
[3873]={"Daily Request: Swamp Full of Danger","Glórellas is in the Court of Celeborn.","Glórellas has asked you to defeat foes in Agarnaith in order to aid adventurers in that plague-ridden reach of Gorgoroth.","Defeat Orcs and Uruks in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Of all the lands of Gorgoroth, it is Agarnaith that I find most offensive. That is a land twisted, corrupted by plague and disease, and it saddens my heart to hear of it. The beauty in that place has been gone for thousands of years, but still it pains me to know of its loss.\
\
'The corruption in Agarnaith has had a withering effect upon the beasts that roam that foul swamp-land; they should be given an end, for that would be a mercy. As for the Orcs and Uruks that lurk, it is not mercy I would wish for them, but an ending that will safe-guard the unfortunate wanderers that must walk in that land. See to both of these aims, and return to me for my thanks and a small reward.'","'If there was some way to heal the hurts of Agarnaith, I would ask you to undertake it. Since there is not, and cannot be, I am content for you to do as you have done against the dangers that lurk within its bounds.\
\
'Return tomorrow and I may have more for you to do on behalf of Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}.'","'The corruption in Agarnaith has had a withering effect upon the beasts that roam that foul swamp-land; they should be given an end, for that would be a mercy. As for the Orcs and Uruks that lurk, it is not mercy I would wish for them, but an ending that will safe-guard the unfortunate wanderers that must walk in that land. See to both of these aims, and return to me for my thanks and a small reward.'","Defeated Orcs and Uruks in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Glórellas in the Court of Celeborn","Defeated beasts in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat beasts in Agarnaith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Glórellas asked you to defeat beasts and Orc-kind in Agarnaith."},
[3874]={"'Very good, very good! Thank you for your hard work, ${PLAYER}. Our smiths will melt down that equipment and use the material as a base for fashioning replacement gear worthy of our heroes.\
\
'Come back tomorrow for more work, my friend. There is always more to be done!'","Vórthi has devised a means of taking Orc-blades and Orc-shields and converting them to use by the dwarves, and needs your help to supply the raw materials.","Collect discarded shields from Udûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Daily Request: The Cart at the Parade Grounds","Collected discarded blades from Udûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'A number of dwarves are hard at work in Gorgoroth, combatting the many dangers that lurk there, but they have encountered an unexpected difficulty: Orc skulls are harder than you'd think! They have been known to dent all but the finest of dwarf weapons. We needed some means of replacing our warriors' gear, as efficiently as possible, and I came up with just such a way!\
\
'I have already set my plan into motion, ${PLAYER}, and it needs only you to apply the finishing touches. If you collect weapons and shields dropped by the Orcs, they can be melted down and used by our smiths. I sent Vágrek to Udûn, and he will wait there with his cart. Search the Orc camps at the valley floor of Udûn for discarded weapons and shields, and load them onto his cart. That gear will be melted down and turned into equipment worthy of our adventurers, and when they are damaged by Orc skulls and weapons, they can be replaced with little trouble!'","Collected discarded shields from Udûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Oh, do not bring the gear to me! Bring it to the cart near the Udûn Foothold!'","Vórthi asked you to search the Orc camps on the valley floor in Udûn for discarded blades and shields that can be turned into dwarf-weapons.","Load the weapons and shields into Vágrek's cart near the Udûn Foothold","Vágrek is by his cart near the Udûn Foothold.","Vórthi is in the Hall Under the Mountain, waiting to hear your report.","Collect discarded blades from Udûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If you collect weapons and shields dropped by the Orcs, they can be melted down and used by our smiths. I sent Vágrek to Udûn, and he will wait there with his cart. Search the Orc camps at the valley floor of Udûn for discarded weapons and shields, and load them onto his cart. That gear will be melted down and turned into equipment worthy of our adventurers, and when they are damaged by Orc skulls and weapons, they can be replaced with little trouble!'","You add your supply of equipment to Vágrek's cart","Talk to Vórthi in the Hall Under the Mountain"},
[3881]={"The Kintai's duty to ensure Nisigím thrives is ceaseless. Though Sívigush threatens to corrupt the last vestiges of purity in the land, they shall endure. To assist them deliver Kinta harvesting tools to Sul Madásh.\
\
Deliver Kinta harvesting tools to Aralath at Sul Madásh.","The Kintai's duty to ensure Nisigím thrives is ceaseless. Though Sívigush threatens to corrupt the last vestiges of purity in the land, they shall endure. To assist them deliver Kinta harvesting tools to Sul Madásh.\
\
Craft Kinta harvesting tools for delivery to Aralath at Sul Madásh.","'We will trade these to those who cannot create their own. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","The Kintai's duty to ensure Nisigím thrives is ceaseless. Though Sívigush threatens to corrupt the last vestiges of purity in the land, they shall endure. To assist them deliver Kinta harvesting tools to Sul Madásh.","Deliver the Kinta harvesting tools to Aralath at Sul Madásh","Diario: Ayudando a una cosecha suave","Collected Kinta harvesting tools (${NUMBER}/8)","Collect Kinta harvesting tools (${NUMBER}/8)"},
[3882]={"Deliver the harvested honey to Lejâni at Zajâna","'Honey has many uses for our people. The sweetness will make our foods more pleasing, and it may also be used as a way to speed along healing.\
\
'Thank you for your efforts.'","Defeat bees in Medân Makhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kighân's recovery requires not only the sword, but also the plowshare. Assist the people by attending to more mundane efforts across the land.\
\
Harvest honeycombs at Medân Makhai.","Daily: An Even Stickier Harvest","Harvest honeycombs at Medân Makha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Honeycombs harvested at Medân Makha (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated bees in Medân Makhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kighân's recovery requires not only the sword, but also the plowshare. Assist the people by attending to more mundane efforts across the land.\
\
Deliver harvested honeycombs from Medân Makhai to Lejâl in Zajâna."},
[3892]={"Daily: Defeat Hâzlur","Defeat the powerful bog-lurker known as Hâzlur wandering Dil-irmíz.","Defeat the bog-lurker Hâzlur","'I hear reports from my scouts that you have accomplished the task of felling Hâzlur.\
\
'We thank you ${CLASS}. That foul beast was a menace that we could not suffer any longer.'","Bôgalekh has asked you to defeat Hâzlur, a powerful bog-lurker spotted in the area.","Return to Bôgalekh in Jadambor in Dil-irmíz to inform them of Hâzlur's defeat.","'Good tidings, ${CLASS}.\
\
'A dangerous bog-lurker by the name of Hâzlur has been spotted wandering Dil-irmíz as of late and I have heard reports from our scouts of the destruction it has been causing.\
\
'We can not let the beast continue to cause harm to the people down here. If you can, gather some allies and deal with this threat.'","Informed Bôgalekh of Hâzlur's defeat","Hâzlur defeated","Return to Bôgalekh to inform them of Hâzlur's defeat"},
[3893]={"Return to Bôgalekh to inform them of Râmakhir's defeat","Bôgalekh has asked you to defeat Râmakhir, a powerful shade spotted in the area.","Informed Bôgalekh of Râmakhir's defeat","'There have been sightings by people here of a vicious shade known as Râmakhir in Dil-irmíz.\
\
'They are quite a dangerous foe, and it is worrisome to have such a monster be so close to Jadambor.\
\
'Reports have claimed that they can be found to the west, but if you do not see them, then destroy their allied shades in the area until they are forced to reveal themselves.\
\
'I would ask that you gather your allies and drive Râmakhir away.'","'We owe you a thanks for driving away Râmakhir.\
\
'Jadambor is now safer as we continue the fight. Take this as a reward.'","Râmakhir defeated","Daily: Defeat Râmakhir","Defeat the shade Râmakhir","Return to Bôgalekh in Jadambor in the flooded undercity to inform them of Râmakhir's defeat.","Defeat the powerful shade known as Râmakhir to the west of Jadambor."},
[3894]={"You hand Kavíra the shade essence you have collected.\
\
'Your kindness warms my heart, ${CLASS}! These will be invaluable in helping our efforts down here. I can not have too many elixirs in my stores. Please take this for your troubles.\
\
'If you happen upon any more I will be glad to take them off your hands.'","Bring the shade essence to Kavíra in Jadambor in western Dil-irmíz.","Essence from defeated shades has many uses. Bring some to Kavíra, the healer in Jadambor, to help resupply their stores.","Collect shade essence in Dil-irmíz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You found shade essence","Bring the shade essence to Kavíra in Jadambor","Daily: Essence for Elixirs","You found shade essence.","You have gathered shade essence from the shades in the area. Kavíra, the healer in Jadambor would have use of these.","Shades can be found to the west of Jadambor.\
\
Collect their essence and bring it to Kavíra in Jadambor.","There are many shades throughout western Dil-irmíz. Kavíra, the healer in Jadambor, would surely be grateful if you restocked their supply of shade essence.","Collected shade essences (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
